+
+### Amendment: classify a known cast before a caller value (#1786)
+
+The #1785 origin rule also governs asks_of_value. It consumes cast_from before
+classifying a function pointer as a caller-supplied value. Otherwise is_function
+of a known namespaced binding omits missing-global guards and throws where the
+namespace is absent; a cast of an ordinary Rust function is also accepted where
+its function item is refused. Unknown pointers supplied by JS retain their value
+checks. One existing origin owner answers all three consumers; no new API or
+representation is introduced. ADR 0262 case A applies to these host questions.
+The retained port regression executes missing/present roots, getter counts and
+refusals; defined-known-cast-read-as-caller-value restores both bugs.
